I thought everybody knew this one.  Human meat tastes like pork.  Smells
like roasting pork when cooking, too.  This is one reason witnesses find
human immolation so disgusting ---- because they smell so *gooood*.  One
begins reflexively to salivate even as one is horrified.  The cognitive
dissonance induced is, I understand, rather shattering.

Mind you, I don't speak from experience.  But all the reports I've ever
read agree on these details.  In one language in the South Pacific, human
meat was called "long pig".  Heinlein and a few other SF writers have been
known to use this idiom in English as a grim joke; that's where I learned it.

