 Profit-making companies frequently buy back some of their stock. It is not
obvious that there is any insurmountable barrier to them buying it all.

 One strong obstacle to unlimited accumulation of wealth has been that any
such plan has until now required human employees to execute the strategy,
and they will always find ways of diverting some of that money to themselves.
 We are approaching the point where such an organization could be automated
without using any direct employees. I suspect that it will still be difficult
for such an organization to dominate the economy, because the costs of
defending that wealth are likely to rise as more people get jealous of its
success (remember Michael Milkin) - unless it manages to keep its existence
a complete secret. Could it already be happening?

