 You misunderstand. Being purchased by individuals who happen to work at top
positions in the company is not the same as the company purchasing its own
stock. When a company buys back its own stock, that stock effectively ceases
to exist, since the stock is just a kind of obligation that the company
created when it originally issued/sold the stock. If it bought back every
share, then there would be no shares to be voted, and it is unclear what
would happen the next time the board of directors was up for re-election.
