Derek Zahn asks:"WHY are people neophobes?"

Neophobia is a very stable meme, and quite useful in a pre-literate
pre-industrial society. It was a successful strategy, and will continue to be
for some time. It was never so successful that it could eliminate neophilia,
but has always been dominant. So its popularity, given history, doesn't seem
any more surprising than the survival of Christianity (in fact, much less
surprising). 
